---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ContactBand from '../components/ContactBand.astro';

const questions = [
  { part: 'alternator', text: 'Which output rating is stamped on the old alternator?' },
  {
    part: 'door mirror',
    text: 'Does the shop need the heated glass, or is the left mirror housing damaged too?',
  },
  { part: 'brake pads', text: 'Can the technician see a wear-sensor lead on the front pads?' },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Parts Relay for distributors | Parts enquiry software for the counter"
  description="Parts enquiry software for the distributor counter. Search by plate or VIN, pick up workshop requests from WhatsApp and hand open questions to the next shift."
>
  <div class="team-page team-dist">
    <section class="team-hero">
      <div class="team-frame">
        <p class="team-label">For distributors</p>
        <h1 tabindex="-1">Parts Relay for distributors</h1>
        <p class="team-hero-note">
          When a workshop rings back, pull up its original enquiry. You can see what it asked for,
          who ran the search and where the last person got to.
        </p>
        <div class="team-actions">
          <a
            class="team-btn"
            href="mailto:contact@reasonandrender.com?subject=Parts%20Relay%20for%20my%20business"
          >
            Talk to our team
          </a>
          <button type="button" class="team-btn team-secondary" data-jump="team-directory">
            Questions by part
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="team-dist-section">
      <div class="team-frame team-overview">
        <div>
          <p class="team-label">Returning a call</p>
          <h2 class="team-h2">When two entries look right</h2>
          <p>
            The vehicle record can still leave you with a choice of alternators. Ask the shop to
            read the rating or number on the old unit. If those match both entries, check which
            connector the technician can see.
          </p>
        </div>
        <ol class="team-numbered">
          <li>
            <span aria-hidden="true">01</span>
            <div>
              <strong>What did they ask for?</strong>Check whether the shop wants a single piece, an
              axle set or a complete assembly. The original wording is useful here.
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span aria-hidden="true">02</span>
            <div>
              <strong>What would settle it?</strong>Ask for the one feature that separates the
              catalogue entries. Keep the answer with this enquiry for the next person on shift.
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span aria-hidden="true">03</span>
            <div>
              <strong>What can the branch supply?</strong>Confirm the quantity and note when the
              branch checked stock before offering a collection or delivery time.
            </div>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section
      class="team-quote-slider"
      aria-label="Questions to ask the workshop"
      data-team-slider
      data-questions={JSON.stringify(questions)}
    >
      <div class="team-slide-copy">
        <div class="team-slide-mark">
          <img src="/assets/symbol.svg" alt="" /> Parts Relay
        </div>
        <div aria-live="off" data-team-slide-body>
          <blockquote>Which output rating is stamped on the old alternator?</blockquote>
          <p>Ask the workshop about the alternator</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="team-slide-controls">
        <button
          type="button"
          data-team-slide="0"
          aria-label="Show alternator question"
          aria-pressed="true"
        >
          <i></i>
        </button>
        <button
          type="button"
          data-team-slide="1"
          aria-label="Show door mirror question"
          aria-pressed="false"
        >
          <i></i>
        </button>
        <button
          type="button"
          data-team-slide="2"
          aria-label="Show brake pads question"
          aria-pressed="false"
        >
          <i></i>
        </button>
        <button
          type="button"
          class="team-play"
          data-team-pause
          aria-label="Pause rotating questions"
          aria-pressed="false"
        >
          Ⅱ
        </button>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="team-dist-section">
      <div class="team-frame">
        <p class="team-label">Reference desk</p>
        <h2 class="team-h2">Where to look next</h2>
        <div class="team-resources">
          <a href="/guides/vehicle-identification/">
            <h3>Vehicle identification</h3>
            <p>Look into a discrepancy between the car and the returned vehicle record.</p>
          </a>
          <a href="/tools/part-details/">
            <h3>Part descriptions</h3>
            <p>Distinguish a single component from a kit in the shop’s description.</p>
          </a>
          <a href="/tools/parts-diagrams/">
            <h3>Assembly diagrams</h3>
            <p>Find the piece a callout points to, including the fittings around it.</p>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="team-dist-section team-directory" id="team-directory" tabindex="-1">
      <div class="team-frame">
        <p class="team-label">Parts reference</p>
        <div class="team-filter-line">
          <h2 class="team-h2">Questions by part</h2>
          <div class="team-filters" role="group" aria-label="Filter by part category">
            <button type="button" aria-pressed="true" data-team-filter="All">
              All
            </button>
            <button type="button" aria-pressed="false" data-team-filter="Brakes">
              Brakes
            </button>
            <button type="button" aria-pressed="false" data-team-filter="Electrical">
              Electrical
            </button>
            <button type="button" aria-pressed="false" data-team-filter="Body">
              Body
            </button>
            <button type="button" aria-pressed="false" data-team-filter="Cooling">
              Cooling
            </button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="team-parts-grid" aria-label="Part checks">
          <details class="team-part" data-team-category="Brakes">
            <summary>
              <svg
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="1.35"
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                aria-hidden="true"
              >
                <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="8.5" />
                <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="2.8" />
                <path d="M6 7.5c1.6-1.5 3-2.2 5-2.3M16.5 17.4l1.6-1.7M14 19l.8-.3" />
              </svg>
              <span>Front pad set</span>
              <i aria-hidden="true">+</i>
            </summary>
            <p>
              Which clips and sensors are in the quoted set? Name anything the shop needs to buy
              separately.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details class="team-part" data-team-category="Electrical">
            <summary>
              <svg
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="1.35"
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                aria-hidden="true"
              >
                <path d="M4 7h16v13H4zM6 7V4h4v3m4 0V4h4v3M7 11h4m-2-2v4m5-2h3" />
              </svg>
              <span>Alternator</span>
              <i aria-hidden="true">+</i>
            </summary>
            <p>
              Look for the rating and the manufacturer’s number on the old alternator. If two units
              still fit the description, check the plug.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details class="team-part" data-team-category="Body">
            <summary>
              <svg
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="1.35"
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                aria-hidden="true"
              >
                <path d="M2 18v-5l7-8h9l3 3v10zM5.5 12l4.3-4.8H17l1.8 2V12zM15 15h3" />
              </svg>
              <span>Left mirror glass</span>
              <i aria-hidden="true">+</i>
            </summary>
            <p>
              Check the shape of the left glass and the terminals for the heater. Does the shop need
              a backing plate too?
            </p>
          </details>
          <details class="team-part" data-team-category="Cooling">
            <summary>
              <svg
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="1.35"
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                aria-hidden="true"
              >
                <rect x="4" y="6" width="16" height="13" rx="1" />
                <path d="M6 4v2m12-2v2M8 8v9m4-9v9m4-9v9M2 9h2m16 7h2" />
              </svg>
              <span>Radiator</span>
              <i aria-hidden="true">+</i>
            </summary>
            <p>
              Where do the hoses meet the radiator? Compare the outlets and mounts with the cooling
              package listed for the car.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details class="team-part" data-team-category="Electrical">
            <summary>
              <svg
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="1.35"
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                aria-hidden="true"
              >
                <path d="M4 7h16v13H4zM6 7V4h4v3m4 0V4h4v3M7 11h4m-2-2v4m5-2h3" />
              </svg>
              <span>Starter motor</span>
              <i aria-hidden="true">+</i>
            </summary>
            <p>
              Read the number on the starter back against the catalogue entry for that engine and
              transmission.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details class="team-part" data-team-category="Body">
            <summary>
              <svg
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="1.35"
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                aria-hidden="true"
              >
                <path d="M2 18v-5l7-8h9l3 3v10zM5.5 12l4.3-4.8H17l1.8 2V12zM15 15h3" />
              </svg>
              <span>Headlamp assembly</span>
              <i aria-hidden="true">+</i>
            </summary>
            <p>
              Use the label to check the side and lighting package. Tell the shop if it needs to
              transfer or order a bulb or control module.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details class="team-part" data-team-category="Cooling">
            <summary>
              <svg
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="1.35"
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                aria-hidden="true"
              >
                <rect x="4" y="6" width="16" height="13" rx="1" />
                <path d="M6 4v2m12-2v2M8 8v9m4-9v9m4-9v9M2 9h2m16 7h2" />
              </svg>
              <span>Coolant hose</span>
              <i aria-hidden="true">+</i>
            </summary>
            <p>
              Trace the hose from one connection to the other on the drawing. Check the branches and
              end fittings before quoting it.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details class="team-part" data-team-category="Brakes">
            <summary>
              <svg
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="1.35"
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                aria-hidden="true"
              >
                <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="8.5" />
                <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="2.8" />
                <path d="M6 7.5c1.6-1.5 3-2.2 5-2.3M16.5 17.4l1.6-1.7M14 19l.8-.3" />
              </svg>
              <span>Rear caliper</span>
              <i aria-hidden="true">+</i>
            </summary>
            <p>
              Match the caliper to the side and parking-brake mechanism on the rear axle. Read the
              supplier’s description for the carrier.
            </p>
          </details>
        </div>
        <span class="team-sr" role="status" data-team-count></span>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="team-dist-section">
      <div class="team-frame team-intake">
        <div>
          <p class="team-label">Search queue</p>
          <h2 class="team-h2">Finding a job your colleague started</h2>
          <p>
            Filter the search queue by requester, status, period or channel, or look up the plate or
            VIN. The same queue holds searches from the counter and from the company’s WhatsApp
            contacts, newest first. Open one to see the vehicle and the parts your colleague found.
          </p>
          <p>
            The owner manages the company and the team. Admins manage WhatsApp contacts and can
            invite viewers. Viewers run searches and see contacts. Ask an owner or admin if a
            workshop needs access.
          </p>
        </div>
        <section class="team-record">
          <h3>What to do with an unfinished search</h3>
          <dl>
            <div>
              <dt>Searching</dt>
              <dd>
                The result shows as soon as it is ready, with no need to reload. You can leave the
                page and the search keeps going.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Vehicle not found</dt>
              <dd>
                The catalogue does not know this plate or VIN. Read it back to the workshop and
                search again.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>No category matched</dt>
              <dd>
                The vehicle was identified, but no part category matched the request. Try a more
                specific part name or its position.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Done</dt>
              <dd>
                Review the original parts and any aftermarket matches. The supplier still has to
                confirm what is available.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Failed</dt>
              <dd>The catalogue could not complete the search. Search again in a moment.</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </section>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="team-dist-section team-reply-sheet">
      <div class="team-frame team-intake">
        <div>
          <p class="team-label">Replying to the adviser</p>
          <h2 class="team-h2">When the kit description leaves something out</h2>
          <p>
            A shop needs a front pad set and a wear sensor. The listing mentions the pads and
            fittings but says nothing about the sensor. You can tell the adviser what you found
            while the supplier checks the pack.
          </p>
          <p>
            For a stock update, give the branch and quantity as well as the time of the check. That
            gives the adviser a basis for arranging collection.
          </p>
        </div>
        <section class="team-record">
          <h3>One way to answer the call</h3>
          <dl>
            <div>
              <dt>What you know</dt>
              <dd>“I’ve found the front set. The supplier lists the pads and the fittings.”</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>What you still need</dt>
              <dd>“There’s no mention of a sensor. I’ll ask whether to price one separately.”</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Who calls back</dt>
              <dd>
                The counter checks the kit contents and available quantity with the supplier, then
                gives the adviser a total.
              </dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </section>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="team-dist-section">
      <div class="team-frame">
        <p class="team-label">Working through a request</p>
        <h2 class="team-h2">From the first call to the return call</h2>
        <div class="team-steps">
          <a href="/tools/enquiry-builder/" style="--team-step: 0">
            <span>01</span>
            <h3>Read the enquiry</h3>
            <small>Receive</small>
            <p>Open the search under the name of the person who sent it.</p>
          </a>
          <a href="/guides/vehicle-identification/" style="--team-step: 1">
            <span>02</span>
            <h3>Check the details</h3>
            <small>Identify</small>
            <p>Read the vehicle description beside the supplied registration.</p>
          </a>
          <a href="/tools/part-details/" style="--team-step: 2">
            <span>03</span>
            <h3>Ask the shop</h3>
            <small>Clarify</small>
            <p>Two entries still fit? Find the marking the technician would need to read.</p>
          </a>
          <a href="/guides/counter/" style="--team-step: 3">
            <span>04</span>
            <h3>Explain the match</h3>
            <small>Reply</small>
            <p>Tell the adviser which reference you can quote and which questions are open.</p>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <ContactBand />
  </div>
</Layout>

<script>
  import '../scripts/distributors.js';
</script>
